// upstream - url called by client
// downstream - actual microservice url
// downstreamscheme -  The protocol used for communication between the gateway and the internal service, set to either http or https


// "ClientIdHeader":  tells Ocelot which header contains the client's ID (X-Client-Id).
// EnableHeaders:     enables rate-limit information in response headers.

// Ocelot uses its default client identification behavior, which can fall back to the request IP address. 
// This means multiple users behind the same IP could share a rate-limit counter.
